{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Let there be</b> — the sense is in their fleeing: before they know the way, let them flee." "<b>And let the angel of YHWH pursue them</b> — until they are not delivered." "<b>And slippery</b> — doubled, like סחרחר, שחרחורת." "<b>And the sense of darkness</b> — thick and smooth, so that the power of the perception of touch can discern it, in the manner of וימש חשך, which is as when the skin is felt, and to be it; like: ויאמש is not correct at all."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {3 "The phrase ולהיותו is obscure; rendered hyper-literally. The arguments about וימש (Gen. 15:12) and ויאמש (Gen. 41:21?) are compressed and remain cryptic."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:36.711771239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}